2026-11-04 01:51 Started. Finding vs design step 5 ('drop the instance'): a dropped MCP::Wiki::Server is NOT freed -- its tool closures capture $self, a cycle through server->tools. Checked with weaken(): leaked; freed once the throwaway server's tools/prompts/resources are emptied. Upstream::Fork therefore empties the throwaway server's lists before letting go, so no Git::Raw repo (or other handle) of the class stays in the hub. Will update the design's Mechanism section to match.

Built. Deviations from the design (all written into the design doc, section 'As built'): (1) step 5 -- the throwaway instance's server lists are emptied before it is let go (cycle via tool closures); a class sharing one server object across instances would lose its lists (none known). (2) Fork also overrides _on_stderr/_on_close/_exit_hint (stderr tail as exit hint, drained before the exit is handled, as Docker::Stdio does) and status_row; Stdio::_spawn's parent half moved into Stdio::_attach. (3) Stdio::start_p leaves a refused spawn 'failed' when _spawn recorded the third exit (needed so the thread refusal counts toward the crash loop). (4) always_on is refused on an in-process class, with the timeouts (k38). (5) Design Tests said tools/list still answers during a crash loop: on the server's own endpoint a failed upstream answers 503 (as for stdio); via /all its tools stay listed. Also found (proposed cards for this board): (a) under Mojo::Reactor::EV, libev's default loop reaps every child at top priority, so Stdio::_on_close's waitpid gets ECHILD and logs 'exited (unknown)' -- exit codes and the exit-127 'is it installed and executable?' hint are lost at random, for stdio, docker CLI and fork alike (t/fork.t works around it with local $SIG{CHLD}='DEFAULT'); (b) command entries silently accept headers/type, url entries env/cwd/args -- the same drift as k38 on the other kinds; (c) _warm_upstream calls start_p on a failed placeholder of a non-perl type, so its build error is logged twice; (d) _drain_stderr is now duplicated in Fork and Docker::Stdio -- could move into Stdio. k39 is not made more urgent: an idle stop only fires with no call in flight.

